target.value:
30 Senior Officials from developing countries;
- 3 New ratifications among developing countries;
- 2 Technical support to experts of LDC and or SIDS on initial UNCAT reporting.

actual.value:
- 112 Senior officials from developing countries participated in CTI events;
- 2 New ratifications: Sudan, Suriname;
- 1 Technical support to experts of LDC and/or SIDS on initial UNCAT-reporting.

2 Briefings:
- Briefing to the Committee against Torture;
- Briefing to the United Nations Voluntary Fund for Victims of Torture;
2 Side Events:
- Side event to the 49th Session of the Human Rights Council;
- Side event to the 31st session of the Commission on Crime Prevention and Criminal Justice (CCPCJ).

- Maldives blog released;
- Indonesia blog released;
- Report on Anti-Torture Standards in common law Africa: Good Practices and Way Forward released;
- 3 Chapters released under the Police Resource toolkit (an additional six Chapters were under development in 2022);
- Paper on the Pacific Towards regional universality of the UN Convention against Torture in the Pacific: A review of the anti-torture legislative and regulatory frameworks in the region developed in 2022, to be released in 2023.
